 "sig": "596646|1791868134525883100|This is what happens when you swallow gum. First, it slides down your esophagus in one piece. In your stomach, acid strips away the sugar and flavor. But the gum base is made of rubbery polymers your body simply can't digest. So no, it doesn't stay inside you for seven years. Your intestines just squeeze it along with everything else. And a few days later, it leaves your body. But swallow lots of gum every day, and it can build into a solid mass that blocks your gut. Doctors have actually had to remove these from kids.",
